%% Invoice lifecycle (BIL): bil_invoice.status. Amounts are fixed once issued (trigger tr_invoice_fixed); Paid and
%% Void never go back. UPCOMING and REFUNDED exist in the schema's CHECK but no code stores them: fees not issued yet
%% are computed for display, and a refund is a bil_refund row while its Invoice stays Paid.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Unpaid : issued — Deposit (FR-APP-02), Balance (FR-ASG-03), next-Term fee (FR-ASG-08), Utility (FR-BIL-04)
  Unpaid --> AwaitingConfirmation : student claims the transfer (FR-BIL-02)
  Overdue --> AwaitingConfirmation : student claims the transfer (FR-BIL-02)
  AwaitingConfirmation --> Paid : Manager confirms the claim (FR-BIL-03)
  AwaitingConfirmation --> Unpaid : Manager rejects the claim, the remaining time continues (FR-BIL-03)
  AwaitingConfirmation --> Overdue : Manager rejects the claim of a debt already past due (FR-BIL-03)
  AwaitingConfirmation --> Void : second rejection of a Deposit or Balance claim (FR-BIL-03)
  Unpaid --> Overdue : due date passes, Utility and charges (job, FR-BIL-05)
  Unpaid --> Void : forfeit, cancelled Application, cancelled next-Term Allocation, or Utility settled from the Utility Deposit at check-out (FR-ASG-11, FR-APP-04, FR-ASG-08, FR-ASG-06)
  Overdue --> Void : cancelled next-Term Allocation, or Utility settled from the Utility Deposit at check-out (FR-ASG-08, FR-ASG-06)
  Paid --> [*]
  Void --> [*]
  note right of Paid : a refund (FR-BIL-06) is a bil_refund row, the Invoice stays Paid

  AwaitingConfirmation : Awaiting confirmation
